  {
    "@id": "https://nac-cna.ca/event/41930#2026-10-10T20:00:00-04:00",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/additionalType": [
      {
        "@id": "http://kg.artsdata.ca/resource/TheatrePerformance"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@value": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@value": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2026-10-10T20:00:00-04:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/endDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2026-10-10T21:15:00-04:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@value": "Black Out Night (BON): Neige sur Abidjan"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@value": "Black Out Night (BON) returns alongside French Theatre's presentation of Neige sur Abidjan, inviting audiences to experience an evening that celebrates culture, conversation, and community. The evening begins with BON Chat, a special pre-show conversation exploring themes of migration, identity, and belonging. Facilitated by Mani Soleymanlou, Artistic Director of French Theatre, and featuring local community voices, this gathering creates space for meaningful dialogue inspired by the play and the experiences of those who have built new lives in Canada. Following the performance, the celebration continues with BON Nuit, where guests are invited to gather over music, food, and conversation inspired by the richness and diversity of African cultures. Come experience an evening where theatre extends beyond the stage, bringing people together through stories, shared experiences, and the belief that culture creates connection. NAC Black Out Nights offer Black audiences and their guests an opportunity to experience performances in community. As always, everyone is welcome to join BON during Neige sur Abidjan, fostering a spirit of inclusivity, dialogue, and celebration. 6:00 to 7:00 pm | BON Chat: Between Two Worlds Join us for a thought-provoking pre-show discussion inspired by the themes of Neige sur Abidjan. Hear from local community voices as they reflect on migration, identity, belonging, and building community in a new home. Free with registration (capacity is limited). Le Salon 8:00 pm | Neige sur Abidjan A moving French Theatre production exploring family, identity, and the complexities of starting over in a new country. Approximately 75 minutes, no intermission. Azrieli Studio. 9:30 pm until late | BON Nuit Continue the evening with an intimate celebration featuring music, conversation, and African-inspired flavours in a relaxed lounge atmosphere. Le Salon"
      }
    ],
